      "message": "feat(ui): browse the holder library in the tool library window\n\nA \"Cutting tools | Holders\" switch heads the tool library window. The\nHolders page lists the built-in holders grouped by spindle taper, the\nmounted machine's taper first and marked, with the clamp, the clamping\nrange, the gauge length, the largest diameter and the number of\ndocument tools that use each holder. A holder opens in a read-only\nview: machine side, tool side, shape, the tools that use it (a click\nopens the tool in the editor) and the outline to scale, cached on its\ninputs. Built-in holders are read-only; user holders and holder edits\nneed the user library of #3645 (U7, #3898).\n\nThe used-by query is in app: tool_body::holder_users and\ntool_body::tools_using_holder, keyed on HolderRef::entry.\n\nNo command is new: browsing is view state.\n\nFixes #3897\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
